{
  "name": "table-week-based",
  "description": "ILLUSTRATIVE: a week_based year (ends on the Saturday nearest the end of January, weeks from Sunday, the NRF anchor) with a table subdivision for the fiscal years 2024 to 2026, each 364 days, split into twelve invented periods of 28 to 35 days that do not follow week boundaries. None of the years has 53 weeks, so has_extra_week is false throughout. The calendar is defined only between the table's first and last entry, so dates, year numbers, shifts, years, labels and dimension ranges outside it are OUT_OF_RANGE. A table subdivision does not split periods into weeks: weeks count from the fiscal year's first day, 'weeks' is null, the parent of a week is the year, and the weeks of a quarter or period are LEVEL_NOT_NESTED.",
  "source": {
    "kind": "oracle",
    "citation": "Independent implementation of the spec in conformance/generators/fiscal_oracle.py, written with Python datetime and no fiscalclock code",
    "url": null,
    "checked_by": "fiscal_oracle.py: Calendar.seq narrowed to the table's years; the table cross-block checks and naming_errors pass"
  },
